  "summary_en": "EESC opinion on the Commission's 2020 AI White Paper. It welcomes the risk-based approach but urges broader high-risk criteria beyond sectors, continuous socio-technical assessment, restrictions on biometric recognition, worker involvement, and opposes legal personality for AI. It also addresses AI use against COVID-19.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Opposes any form of legal personality for AI",
   "Calls for sector-independent criteria for intrinsically high-risk AI",
   "Recommends continuous socio-technical assessment rather than one-off conformity assessment",
   "Biometric recognition only under proven, controlled, strict conditions; ban widespread surveillance use",
   "Early social dialogue with workers before introducing AI at workplaces"
  ],
